+<!-- seo:body --><noscript><section class="crawl-text"><h1>Kshana Studio</h1><p>Kshana Studio runs Kshana, the open-source PNT (positioning, navigation and timing) resilience simulator, in your browser: the engine runs locally as WebAssembly, so nothing is installed and nothing is uploaded. Pick a GNSS (global navigation satellite system) jamming, spoofing, clock holdover, integrity or lunar navigation scenario, tune it, replay it, compare runs, sweep a parameter and download a reproducible report. It needs JavaScript.</p><h2>Scenarios it runs (185)</h2><ul><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=acm-link&amp;tab=overview">acm-link</a>: DVB-S2 adaptive coding and modulation (ACM) along one satellite&#x27;s passes over one station.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aocs-slew&amp;tab=overview">aocs-slew</a>: Reaction-wheel attitude slew under MRP feedback, closed on the true state.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aocs-slew-mekf&amp;tab=overview">aocs-slew-mekf</a>: Reaction-wheel attitude slew under MRP feedback, closed on an MEKF estimate.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aperture-duty-cycle&amp;tab=overview">aperture-duty-cycle</a>: Aperture duty-cycle demonstrator (ground segment &amp; operations).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=araim-gps-galileo&amp;tab=timeseries">araim-gps-galileo</a>: Dual-constellation ARAIM availability: GPS + Galileo evaluated with the advanced</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=araim-reference-check&amp;tab=overview">araim-reference-check</a>: The engine&#x27;s ARAIM protection levels against the WG-C subgroup&#x27;s OWN worked examples.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=ascent-losses&amp;tab=overview">ascent-losses</a>: Gravity-turn ascent losses of an ILLUSTRATIVE two-stage kerosene/oxygen launcher (no real</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=attitude-budget&amp;tab=overview">attitude-budget</a>: 3-DOF attitude &amp; pointing error budget demonstrator (pre-hardware AOCS/GNC).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=automotive-urban-canyon&amp;tab=holdover">automotive-urban-canyon</a>: Road vehicle through an urban canyon: GNSS/INS dead-reckoning across an underpass and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-jam-spoof-holdover-integrity&amp;tab=campaign&amp;play=1">campaign-jam-spoof-holdover-integrity</a>: A chained mission: nominal, jamming, spoofing, GNSS loss with clock holdover and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-monte-carlo-clock-holdover&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-monte-carlo-clock-holdover</a>: A seeded Monte Carlo ensemble through a campaign, on a case with a closed form.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-optimize-link-budget&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-optimize-link-budget</a>: An optimisation through a campaign: the link-budget example&#x27;s X-band link</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-shared-jammer-sea-road&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-shared-jammer-sea-road</a>: Cross-domain composition: one jammer, two platforms. A ship in the Gulf of Finland</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-spectrum-holdover-integrity&amp;tab=campaign&amp;play=1">campaign-spectrum-holdover-integrity</a>: A chained mission driven by the L-band spectrum: a chirp jammer takes GPS L1 C/A and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-sweep-jammer-power&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-sweep-jammer-power</a>: A parameter sweep through a campaign: the jamming example&#x27;s receiver (52 N, 4 E,</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-classical-pilot-signals&amp;tab=leo-signal">celeste-iod-classical-pilot-signals</a>: Celeste IOD signal designs: the frequency bands and the &quot;Classical Pilot&quot; signal</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-end-to-end&amp;tab=leo-chain">celeste-iod-end-to-end</a>: Celeste IOD end to end (optional preset): the E5 configuration #1 signal -&gt; a Celeste IOD</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-fused-pvt&amp;tab=leo-positioning">celeste-iod-fused-pvt</a>: GNSS positioning joined by the two ESA Celeste in-orbit demonstration satellites.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=cislunar-arc-recovery&amp;tab=overview">cislunar-arc-recovery</a>: Independent-estimator test of the cislunar arc-length observability threshold (R6, paper B).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=cislunar-observability&amp;tab=overview">cislunar-observability</a>: Planar cislunar constellation observability over a tracking arc (P6).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=clock-ensemble&amp;tab=timeseries">clock-ensemble</a>: Monte Carlo ensemble of the clock-holdover scenario.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=clock-holdover&amp;tab=holdover">clock-holdover</a>: Kshana reference scenario: 2 h run, 10 min GNSS sync then ~1.8 h denied.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=clock-holdover-labsr&amp;tab=holdover">clock-holdover-labsr</a>: Variant: laboratory-grade strontium optical clock vs CSAC.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=combined-altpnt&amp;tab=overview">combined-altpnt</a>: Combined gravity + magnetic + terrain GPS-denied navigator — fused alt-PNT.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=conflict-resilience&amp;tab=overview">conflict-resilience</a>: Layered-PNT conflict resilience (paper P7).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=constellation-multi-gnss-coverage&amp;tab=coverage&amp;play=1">constellation-multi-gnss-coverage</a>: Multi-constellation coverage: the four global navigation satellite systems (GNSS) together,</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=contact-schedule&amp;tab=overview">contact-schedule</a>: Ground-contact planning: three illustrative satellites over three illustrative stations for</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=earth-gnss-lunar&amp;tab=overview">earth-gnss-lunar</a>: Earth-GNSS reception at lunar distance.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=entry-heating-stardust&amp;tab=overview">entry-heating-stardust</a>: Stardust sample-return capsule entry: the published case the `entry-heating` kind is checked</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=eo-coverage&amp;tab=overview">eo-coverage</a>: Earth-observation payload footprint &amp; coverage demonstrator (SMAD space triangle).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=eo-radiometry&amp;tab=overview">eo-radiometry</a>: Nadir imager radiometry and image quality for an ILLUSTRATIVE small Earth-observation camera</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=ephemeris&amp;tab=ground">ephemeris</a>: Ephemeris &amp; ground track — &quot;where is the satellite right now&quot;.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=europa-surface-pnt&amp;tab=body-pnt">europa-surface-pnt</a>: Positioning a lander on Europa: the Jovian-moon case.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=fusion-pnt&amp;tab=holdover">fusion-pnt</a>: Joint sensor-fusion PNT: a single Kalman filter is the navigator, fusing the</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=fusion-pnt-coupled&amp;tab=holdover">fusion-pnt-coupled</a>: Coupled joint sensor-fusion PNT: the same suites and GNSS outage as `fusion-pnt.toml`, but</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ins&amp;tab=holdover">gnss-ins</a>: Loosely-coupled GNSS/INS: the three-axis strapdown navigator disciplined by a</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ins-aviation&amp;tab=holdover">gnss-ins-aviation</a>: Aviation GNSS/INS with tight coupling: a light aircraft takes off, climbs at 6 deg, levels</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ins-maritime&amp;tab=holdover">gnss-ins-maritime</a>: Maritime GNSS/INS: a vessel at 8 m/s (about 15.5 knots) weaving through full circles at</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ins-rail&amp;tab=holdover">gnss-ins-rail</a>: Rail GNSS/INS with tight coupling: a train runs between stops at 30 m/s with gentle 20 deg</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-sim-container-terminal-skyline&amp;tab=overview">gnss-sim-container-terminal-skyline</a>: Pseudoranges and RAIM for a straddle carrier on a container quay, with ship-to-shore</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-sim-raim&amp;tab=overview">gnss-sim-raim</a>: Measurement-domain GNSS simulation: pseudoranges with ionospheric and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-formation-heo&amp;tab=overview">gnss-ssv-formation-heo</a>: Relative navigation of a three-craft formation in the booklet&#x27;s highly elliptical orbit.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-heo&amp;tab=overview">gnss-ssv-heo</a>: A highly elliptical orbit through the GNSS orbits: what a user sees from perigee to apogee.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-lunar-weak&amp;tab=overview">gnss-ssv-lunar-weak</a>: GNSS on a lunar transfer, with a weak-signal receiver that earns its sensitivity.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-nav-lunar&amp;tab=overview">gnss-ssv-nav-lunar</a>: Onboard GNSS navigation on the way to the Moon: an extended Kalman filter on pseudoranges alone.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-shell&amp;tab=overview">gnss-ssv-shell</a>: GNSS signal availability on the upper-SSV shell: the booklet&#x27;s global metric, at a size that runs in a second.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gps-denied-gravity-nav&amp;tab=overview">gps-denied-gravity-nav</a>: 60-minute GPS-denied gravity-map-matching benchmark (quantum alt-PNT).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gps-denied-gravity-nav-egm2008&amp;tab=overview">gps-denied-gravity-nav-egm2008</a>: 60-minute GPS-denied gravity-map-matching benchmark on the REAL gravity field (WP-10, RM-17).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gravity-map-error-mc&amp;tab=overview">gravity-map-error-mc</a>: Map-error Monte Carlo on the 60-minute GPS-denied gravity-map benchmark (WP-10, RM-15).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=gravity-map-nav&amp;tab=overview">gravity-map-nav</a>: Quantum gravity-map-matching navigation scenario (GPS-denied alt-PNT).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=holdover-test-example&amp;tab=overview">holdover-test-example</a>: Holdover test, ingestion example: a time-error record scored by the holdover-test kind</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=holdover-test-ptp4l&amp;tab=overview">holdover-test-ptp4l</a>: Holdover test of a linuxptp log: the same four steps as holdover-test-example.toml, with the record</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=hybrid-optical-rf&amp;tab=overview">hybrid-optical-rf</a>: Heterogeneous optical + RF PNT joint availability / precision / integrity (P5).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=hybrid-pnt&amp;tab=holdover">hybrid-pnt</a>: Hybrid PNT capstone: all-quantum suite (optical clock + cold-atom IMU + optical ISL</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=hybrid-ukf&amp;tab=overview">hybrid-ukf</a>: 17-state hybrid quantum + classical tightly-coupled GNSS/INS UKF (MODELLED).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=impairment-eval&amp;tab=overview">impairment-eval</a>: Machine-learning RF-impairment detection evaluation testbed (ESA AO/1-13494 demonstrator).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=imu-deadreckoning&amp;tab=holdover">imu-deadreckoning</a>: Dead-reckoning during GNSS outage: cold-atom quantum accelerometer vs navigation-grade.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=ins-trn-coast&amp;tab=overview">ins-trn-coast</a>: INS/TRN coasting error model — position error against coast duration, and the coast</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=integrity-harbour-approach&amp;tab=timeseries">integrity-harbour-approach</a>: ARAIM availability for a vessel entering a harbour: the `integrity` kind with a ground-site</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=integrity-raim&amp;tab=timeseries">integrity-raim</a>: GNSS integrity (RAIM) availability over a GPS-like constellation.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=jamming-demo&amp;tab=signal">jamming-demo</a>: RF jamming: a ground-based broadband jammer denying GNSS to a nearby receiver.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=jamming-harbour-approach-skyline&amp;tab=signal">jamming-harbour-approach-skyline</a>: A ship entering a harbour under a shore jammer, with the quay buildings ahead taking the</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=l-band-waterfall-jamming&amp;tab=spectrum&amp;play=1">l-band-waterfall-jamming</a>: L-band waterfall under jamming: the whole Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS)</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=launch-window&amp;tab=overview">launch-window</a>: Launch-window &amp; ascent geometry demonstrator (mission analysis, trade-study tier).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-band-trade&amp;tab=leo-signal">leo-band-trade</a>: LEO-PNT band trade, UHF to wide C band: what a low Earth orbit (LEO) positioning,</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-doppler-positioning&amp;tab=leo-positioning">leo-doppler-positioning</a>: Positioning from LEO Doppler alone, over a generic LEO navigation constellation.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-data-services&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-data-services</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: additional PNT data services in the navigation message.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-fused-pnt-sisre&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-fused-pnt-sisre</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: MEO + LEO fused PNT.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-indoor-uhf&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-indoor-uhf</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: indoor navigation with UHF.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-iot-eirp&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-iot-eirp</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: low-energy positioning for the Internet of Things (IoT) and mobile.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-ntn-bandwidth&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-ntn-bandwidth</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: 5G/6G non-terrestrial network (NTN) compatibility.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-ppp-altitude&amp;tab=campaign">leo-focus-ppp-altitude</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: high-accuracy positioning (precise point positioning, PPP).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-focus-science-iono-sounding&amp;tab=leo-pass">leo-focus-science-iono-sounding</a>: LEO-PNT focus area: LEO-PNT science, ionosphere sounding from the dual-band delay.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-indoor-uhf&amp;tab=leo-pass">leo-indoor-uhf</a>: Indoor LEO-PNT: why a UHF carrier reaches inside a building when L, S and C bands struggle.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=leo-iot-energy&amp;